---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, buildBreadcrumbLd } from '../lib/seo';

const title = 'Terms of Service | pictojxl.com';
const description =
  'Terms of Service for pictojxl.com — acceptable use, intellectual property, disclaimers, and limitation of liability for our browser-based JXL converter.';

const jsonLd = [
  buildBreadcrumbLd([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Terms of Service', path: '/terms-of-service' },
  ]),
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/terms-of-service" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <LegalPage
    title="Terms of Service"
    description="The rules and limitations that apply when you use pictojxl.com."
  >
    <p>
      These Terms of Service (“Terms”) govern your access to and use of
      <a href={absoluteUrl('/')}>pictojxl.com</a> (the “Service”), operated by
      <strong>Webwise Private Company Ltd</strong>, a United States company (“Webwise,” “we,” “us,”
      or “our”). By accessing or using the Service, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree,
      do not use the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Description of the Service</h2>
    <p>
      pictojxl.com provides a browser-based tool for converting and inspecting images in JPEG XL
      (JXL) and related formats. Processing is performed locally on your device using WebAssembly
      and related browser technologies. We do not host a server-side conversion pipeline for your
      image files.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Acceptable Use Policy</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Use automated bots, scrapers, or scripts to abuse, overload, or disrupt the Service;</li>
      <li>Attempt denial-of-service attacks or interfere with other users’ access;</li>
      <li>
        Use the Service to process illegal, malicious, exploitative, or otherwise unlawful content;
      </li>
      <li>
        Convert or distribute copyrighted material unless you own the rights or have permission to
        do so;
      </li>
      <li>Attempt to reverse engineer, compromise, or misuse the site infrastructure.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may suspend or block access if we reasonably believe these Terms have been violated.</p>

    <h2>3. Intellectual Property Rights</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Your content:</strong> You retain 100% ownership and copyright of all images you
      convert or process with the Service. Because files are processed on your device and are not
      uploaded to our servers, we claim no ownership, license, or residual rights in your images.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Our content:</strong> The Service’s branding, UI, documentation, and software
      (excluding your images and third-party open components used under their licenses) are owned by
      Webwise or its licensors and are protected by applicable intellectual property laws.
    </p>

    <h2>4. “As-Is” Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
    <p>
      THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED ON AN “AS IS” AND “AS AVAILABLE” BASIS WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND,
      WHETHER EXPRESS, IMPLIED, OR STATUTORY, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF
      MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.
    </p>
    <p>
      Without limiting the foregoing, we do not warrant that conversions will be error-free, that
      output quality will meet your expectations, or that the Service will operate uninterrupted on
      every device. Extremely large or high-resolution files may exceed your local hardware or
      browser memory limits and may cause slowdowns, failed conversions, or browser crashes. You
      are solely responsible for keeping backups of important files.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <p>
      TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, WEBWISE PRIVATE COMPANY LTD AND ITS DIRECTORS,
      EMPLOYEES, AND AFFILIATES SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL,
      CONSEQUENTIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, REVENUE, DATA, GOODWILL,
      OR BUSINESS OPPORTUNITY, ARISING OUT OF OR RELATED TO YOUR USE OF (OR INABILITY TO USE) THE
      SERVICE—EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our total liability for any claim arising from the Service shall not exceed the greater of (a)
      the amount you paid us for the Service in the twelve (12) months preceding the claim (if any),
      or (b) zero U.S. dollars if the Service was provided free of charge.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      The Service may display advertisements or load third-party scripts (for example Google
      AdSense). Your interactions with third parties are governed by their own terms and policies.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Our collection and use of information is described in our
      <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes to the Terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these Terms from time to time. The “Last updated” date will change when we do.
      Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Governing Law</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by the laws of the United States and the State in which Webwise
      Private Company Ltd maintains its principal place of business, without regard to conflict of
      law principles, except where mandatory consumer protections in your jurisdiction apply.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Webwise Private Company Ltd (USA)<br />
      Email: <a href="mailto:support@pictojxl.com">support@pictojxl.com</a>
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</Layout>
